# Ductective — environment template
#
# ⚠️  THIS FILE IS TRACKED BY GIT. Placeholders only — never real values.
#     Real keys go in `.env`, which is gitignored. See .gitignore:11-12.
#
# The split below enforces acceptance criterion 3 in .pipeline/00-brief.md:
# no API key may be present in the client bundle.
#
# Expo inlines any var prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ into the shipped app bundle.
# Anything without that prefix stays server-side and must be set as a
# Supabase Edge Function secret, not read from this file at runtime.
# Run A may rename these — if it does, it updates this file too.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client-safe (ships in the app bundle — anon key is RLS-protected by design)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Origin only. No trailing path — supabase-js appends /rest/v1 itself.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-side only (Edge Function secrets — must never reach the client)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Bypasses row-level security. Treat as a database root password.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# aistudio.google.com — answer generation. Note there is no hard spend cap on a
# Google key the way there is on an Anthropic one; see SETUP-BLOCKERS.md H2.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# voyageai.com — embeddings for the knowledge base.
VOYAGE_API_KEY=

# Local diagnostic core for development (npm run serve). Unset = the app uses
# mock answers. Use your LAN address, not localhost, for a phone on the network.
EXPO_PUBLIC_DIAGNOSE_URL=

# ST-02 / OQ1 — test paths only. `1` lets /diagnose run WITHOUT unit context
# (no equipment, no documentIds), which the app path must never do: unitless
# non-hazard requests get the `unit_required` shape. Leave unset in normal use.
ALLOW_UNSCOPED_DIAGNOSE=

# ST-09 — optional overrides for the serve-path instrumentation files.
# Defaults live beside the server: scripts/quota-ledger.json (model calls per
# day against the 20/day Gemini free-tier budget) and scripts/request-log.jsonl
# (one line of numbers per request — `npm run metrics` summarizes a batch into
# p50/p95 latency and mean cost with/without cache). Neither file ever
# contains symptom text, image bytes, or keys.
QUOTA_LEDGER_FILE=
REQUEST_LOG_FILE=
